@node Top
@top typst-watch

typst-watch starts a buffer-local @command{typst watch} process for
Typst buffers.  Major-mode preview keybindings open generated PDFs in a
configurable viewer when needed, without calling the original browser preview
command.

@menu
* Installation::
* Usage::
* Configuration::
* Development::
@end menu

@node Installation
@chapter Installation

Place typst-watch.el on your load-path, then load it:

@lisp
(require 'typst-watch)
@end lisp

Enable automatic watching for Typst buffers:

@lisp
(typst-watch-auto-mode 1)
@end lisp

@node Usage
@chapter Usage

Use @kbd{M-x typst-watch-mode} to start or stop a buffer-local
@command{typst watch} process.

When typst-watch-mode is enabled, it starts @command{typst watch} by default.
When the mode is disabled, or when the Typst buffer dies, it stops the
buffer-local watch process.

When typst-watch-auto-mode is enabled, typst-watch-mode is enabled in
typst-ts-mode and typst-mode buffers.  Preview commands listed in
typst-watch-preview-commands are remapped to typst-watch-preview, which opens
the PDF viewer when needed.  Compile-only commands remain owned by the major
mode.

@node Configuration
@chapter Configuration

Set typst-watch-pdf-viewer to force a viewer:

@lisp
(setq typst-watch-pdf-viewer "zathura")
@end lisp

When typst-watch-pdf-viewer is nil, typst-watch tries @command{zathura}
and then @command{evince}.  Change the fallback with
typst-watch-fallback-pdf-viewer.

Set typst-watch-typst-command when Typst is not on PATH.

Set typst-watch-start-on-enable to nil to disable automatic watcher startup
while keeping preview integration.

Set typst-watch-preview-commands to change which major-mode preview command
keybindings open the PDF viewer.

Set typst-watch-output-file-function to customise the output PDF path.
The function receives the Typst source path and must return the PDF path.

@node Development
@chapter Development

Run the full local gate:

@example
make all
@end example

This byte-compiles the package with warnings as errors, runs the ERT tests,
runs checkdoc, and builds this info manual.

